      "text": "Section 1. The Deputy Mayor for Finance and Economic Development, whose office is established pursuant to Executive Order No. 2, dated January 1, 1994, hereby is authorized to perform any function, power or duty of the Mayor in relation to the submission of information to the State Comptroller, in accordance with section 980-g of the General Municipal Law, in connection with the establishment or extension of a business improvement district or the amendment of the district plan of a business improvement district, including but not limited to the power to sign and submit the statement required pursuant to paragraph four of subdivision (b) of section 980-g of the General Municipal Law.",
